  "complexity": 3,
  "title": "H3: bus_create_task echoes a compact row instead of the full task; bus_read gains parent and ids filters so a Planner scans one goal without pulling every task",
  "spec": "Goal T-1515 (human 2026-10-02 01:15), plan label H3. Problem: orchestrator/bus_mcp.py bus_create_task returns bus.create_task's full task dict, so every filed spec (3-6 KB) comes straight back into the Planner's context; bus_read(status_not='done') with no parent filter returned 212k characters this session because it walks every task of every goal.\n\nFacts (main c4dbf2d):\n- bus_mcp.py: bus_create_task(...) -> dict returns bus.create_task(...) unchanged; bus_read(task_id, status, status_not, role, compact=True, full=False) -> bus.read(status=..., status_not=..., role=..., compact=compact and not full).\n- bus.py: _compact_row(t) is the skimmable row {id, parent, role, status, complexity, tier, title[:90], depends_on, hold_reason, reason[:120], merged_into, assigned_to, has_result, result_summary[:160]}; read(tid=None, status=None, status_not=None, role=None, compact=False) filters by status/status_not/role after loading every task via get(); it prints 'bus.read: skipped N unreadable rows' to stderr.\n- tests/test_bus.py and tests/test_mcp.py exercise bus_mcp tools (grep 'bus_mcp' in tests/).\n\nChange:\n1. bus_mcp.bus_create_task returns bus._compact_row(created) plus 'acceptance_count', 'scope_count' and 'spec_chars' (ints) so the Planner sees the id, title, depends_on and sizes but not the spec it just wrote. bus.create_task itself is unchanged (CLI and daemon callers keep the full dict).\n2. bus.read gains keyword parameters parent: str | None = None and ids: list[str] | None = None: parent keeps tasks whose 'parent' equals it; ids keeps only those ids (loaded directly via get, skipping unknown ids and counting them in the skipped notice, instead of walking every row). Both compose with status/status_not/role. bus_mcp.bus_read exposes both (parent: str | None = None, ids: list[str] | None = None) and its docstring tells the Planner to pass parent=<goal id> for a goal scan and ids=[...] for a handful of tasks.\n3. bus_mcp.bus_read with no task_id, no parent, no ids and more than [bus].read_warn_rows rows (default 200, read from pool_config().get('bus', {}) lazily; fall back to 200 without a pool) prepends one compact row-shaped dict {'notice': 'N rows; pass parent=<goal id> or ids=[...] to narrow'} to the list. The notice does not change the list type.\n\nTests that assert the old behaviour (SPEC RULE): any test asserting bus_mcp.bus_create_task returns the spec or events (grep 'bus_create_task' in tests/) is updated to assert the compact echo; tests calling bus.read positionally keep working (new parameters are keyword-only). Run tests/test_bus.py and tests/test_mcp.py.\n\nRollback: one `git revert` of the merge commit. Out of scope: daemon.py, cli.py, tool_catalog.py (the tool names and categories are unchanged).\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1515. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests. Locate every insertion point by symbol, never by line number.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_bus_create_task_echoes_compact_row: passes: bus_mcp.bus_create_task(...) with a 4000-character spec returns a dict with id, title, parent, depends_on, status 'queued', acceptance_count, scope_count and spec_chars == 4000, and no 'spec', 'events' or 'acceptance' key; bus.get(id)['spec'] is the full spec",
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_bus_read_parent_and_ids_filters: passes: with tasks under two parents, bus.read(parent=P) returns only P's children (composing with status_not='done'), bus.read(ids=[a, b, 'T-9999']) returns a and b in id order and reports the unknown id in the skipped notice, and bus_mcp.bus_read(parent=P) returns compact rows of P's children only",
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_bus_read_unfiltered_notice_above_warn_rows: passes: bus_mcp.bus_read() with more rows than [bus].read_warn_rows (set to 3 in the test cfg) returns a list whose first element is the notice dict naming the row count and the parent/ids hint; with parent set no notice is added",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
